The function loops over the events and keeps two dictionaries. One holds the entry time of every car currently parked, and the other holds the fee computed for each car that leaves. For an enter, the car's time is recorded only if it is not already parked. For an exit, the fee is paid out of the parked dictionary for a parked car and ignored for an unregistered one.

Both dictionaries begin empty. Every time a car enters that is not already parked it gets a new entry time; the overlapping enter for a parked car simply does nothing. Every time a car exits that is parked, both the parked dictionary and the fee dictionary receive a record, and the exit-time minus enter-time difference at the given rate is the fee for that car, computed when the event occurs. The exit dictionary is returned, so an entry is absent unless a car successfully left and otherwise the records to resolve overlap are gone.

